        "summary": "Y(III) is diamagnetic, so DC magnetism probes the {Cr3} subsystem. χT at 300 K is 5.4 cm3 K mol−1 (expected 5.6 for three isolated Cr(III)). Curie-like behaviour persists to ~5 K; Cr–Cr exchange is extremely weak. Reduced magnetization isotherms overlay with saturation 8.9 NμB at low T, matching three isolated S = 3/2 Cr(III) ions (g ≈ 2).",
